Subject: [PATCH] Cache translated preset shaders

The HLSL-to-GLSL translation of a preset's warp and composite shaders took about
13 ms per preset on the render thread even when the linked program itself came
from the program cache (patch 0002), because that cache is keyed by the GLSL
source. The translated GLSL is now cached as well, keyed by everything the
translation depends on (shader type, preset code, sampler and texsize
declarations), shared by all instances and threads and bounded to 64 entries.
ProjectM TV's background instance translates the next preset first, so the
render thread goes straight to the cached program.

---
diff --git a/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/MilkdropShader.cpp b/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/MilkdropShader.cpp
index fa769d5c7..8e0018ccf 100644
--- a/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/MilkdropShader.cpp
+++ b/src/libprojectM/MilkdropPreset/MilkdropShader.cpp
